  "title": "Native emergence is approximable except where Fibonacci meets a twist",
  "subject": "Which knots make approximate counting of native networks tractable",
  "conclusion": "Given McQuillan's winding theorem, native counting with pins is approximable for the 26 windable knots, because the knot axiom K2 is his terraced condition; with the four topological knots this settles 28 of 34. The six left open are the Fibonacci knot with one or two negated places, which escape winding and holography and freeze native trees, as not-all-equal and parity do.",
